@title Claude Chan
# Claude Chan (Claude娘, orange hair and chrysanthemum motif) as a static 3D figure.
# Built from her design sheet: front/side/back views, outfit pieces and accessories.
# Every part is a parametric surface (X,Y,Z,u,u0,u1,v,v0,v1). z is up, she faces -y, and +x is her left.
# Generated by generate.py in this folder: helper functions first, then the head, hair, outfit and props.

# Helpers. fw places a local shape (p,q,r) in a frame: origin o, axes (i,j,k) given per coordinate.
fw(p,q,r,o,i,j,k)=o+p*i+q*j+r*k
# Capsule profile: u runs 0..pi from one end to the other, radius r0 -> r1, rounded ends.
cf(u)=(1-cos(u))/2
cr(u,r0,r1)=(r0+(r1-r0)*cf(u))*sqrt(sqrt(1-cos(u)^4))

//Head
# The head is sculpted from parts: a face mask, the cranium under the hair, the underside of the jaw,
# the neck and the ears. The face mask is the face designed in Blender (bface.py), a stack of horizontal arcs, one per
# height h. Each arc runs from the side of the head around the front to the other side: half-width fwd(h), depth fd(h),
# and a superellipse exponent fq(h) that makes it flat in front and turn quickly at the cheeks. fpl(h) is the profile of
# the face seen from the side (forehead, the dip between the eyes, the plane of the cheeks and mouth, a small chin),
# fws(h) the outline seen from the front (level across the eyes and cheekbones, a soft V to a small, rounded chin), and
# fcr(h) rounds both into the chin. fr adds the small features: the nose, the hollows under the brows, the cheeks, the
# lips, the line of the mouth and the chin. fy(p,h) is the y of the skin at x=p, z=h.
smn(a,b,c)=(a+b-sqrt((a-b)^2+c^2))/2
fpl(h)=(-0.44601)+(-2.41681)*(h-10.9225)+406.43605*max(0,h-10.9225)^3+(-689.48633)*max(0,h-10.9479)^3+307.03177*max(0,h-10.985)^3+(-34.04263)*max(0,h-11.0284)^3+(-2.57177)*max(0,h-11.0764)^3+13.96126*max(0,h-11.1282)^3+4.44919*max(0,h-11.1833)^3+(-0.62763)*max(0,h-11.2412)^3+(-11.99939)*max(0,h-11.3016)^3+14.42135*max(0,h-11.3643)^3+(-11.30274)*max(0,h-11.4292)^3+0.89891*max(0,h-11.496)^3+(-2.09427)*max(0,h-11.5647)^3+2.83129*max(0,h-11.6351)^3+4.64741*max(0,h-11.7072)^3+2.25573*max(0,h-11.7808)^3+(-1.86372)*max(0,h-11.856)^3+(-3.93755)*max(0,h-11.9325)^3+(-3.32541)*max(0,h-12.0104)^3+7.96368*max(0,h-12.0896)^3+(-3.98487)*max(0,h-12.1701)^3+1.6753*max(0,h-12.2518)^3+(-1.37052)*max(0,h-12.3347)^3+7.07788*max(0,h-12.4187)^3+(-17.4028)*max(0,h-12.5038)^3
fws(h)=0.04748+3.68027*(h-10.9225)+(-347.36634)*max(0,h-10.9225)^3+530.80763*max(0,h-10.9479)^3+(-157.73993)*max(0,h-10.985)^3+(-15.10535)*max(0,h-11.0284)^3+(-11.17078)*max(0,h-11.0764)^3+(-1.67377)*max(0,h-11.1282)^3+5.72638*max(0,h-11.1833)^3+(-2.47891)*max(0,h-11.2412)^3+(-5.74557)*max(0,h-11.3016)^3+5.08571*max(0,h-11.3643)^3+7.94761*max(0,h-11.4292)^3+(-11.44934)*max(0,h-11.496)^3+4.27057*max(0,h-11.5647)^3+0.33636*max(0,h-11.6351)^3+(-1.8734)*max(0,h-11.7072)^3+4.37981*max(0,h-11.7808)^3+(-3.84179)*max(0,h-11.856)^3+(-6.71246)*max(0,h-11.9325)^3+4.40643*max(0,h-12.0104)^3+5.87322*max(0,h-12.0896)^3+(-4.03616)*max(0,h-12.1701)^3+0.20115*max(0,h-12.2518)^3+0.08209*max(0,h-12.3347)^3+(-6.41282)*max(0,h-12.4187)^3+15.33585*max(0,h-12.5038)^3
fds(h)=0.05602+4.34271*(h-10.9225)+(-409.89224)*max(0,h-10.9225)^3+626.35283*max(0,h-10.9479)^3+(-186.1326)*max(0,h-10.985)^3+(-17.82593)*max(0,h-11.0284)^3+(-13.17623)*max(0,h-11.0764)^3+(-1.99294)*max(0,h-11.1282)^3+6.81876*max(0,h-11.1833)^3+(-3.14026)*max(0,h-11.2412)^3+(-6.02227)*max(0,h-11.3016)^3+3.32005*max(0,h-11.3643)^3+5.15649*max(0,h-11.4292)^3+(-3.73305)*max(0,h-11.496)^3+12.8813*max(0,h-11.5647)^3+(-10.91068)*max(0,h-11.6351)^3+(-4.31167)*max(0,h-11.7072)^3+(-2.40638)*max(0,h-11.7808)^3+2.04622*max(0,h-11.856)^3+3.95203*max(0,h-11.9325)^3+3.44179*max(0,h-12.0104)^3+(-8.15838)*max(0,h-12.0896)^3+4.07712*max(0,h-12.1701)^3+(-1.68278)*max(0,h-12.2518)^3+1.25106*max(0,h-12.3347)^3+(-7.03235)*max(0,h-12.4187)^3+17.68152*max(0,h-12.5038)^3
fcr(h)=sqrt(max(0,h-10.92246)/(h-10.87128))
fwd(h)=fws(h)*fcr(h)
fd(h)=fds(h)*fcr(h)
fdz(h)=((h-11.694)/8.53+0.11111*min(0,(h-11.694)/8.53))
fdt(h)=max(0,(h-11.90725)/0.81888)^2*(3-2*max(0,(h-11.90725)/0.81888))
fq(h)=(0.36-0.08*exp(-(fdz(h)/0.022)^2)+0.06/(1+exp((fdz(h)+0.05)/0.01)))*(1-fdt(h))+0.5*fdt(h)
fnc(h)=min(1,max(0,(11.76224-h)/0.31987))
fno(h)=0.05459*fnc(h)^1.4*exp(-(min(0,h-11.44236)/0.03583)^2)
fns(h)=0.02559+0.03071*fnc(h)^1.5
fr(p,h)=-fno(h)*exp(-(p/fns(h))^2)+0.01024*exp(-((abs(p)-0.37105)/0.1706)^2-((h-11.71106)/0.11089)^2)-0.02559*exp(-((abs(p)-0.39238)/0.16207)^2-((h-11.42957)/0.15354)^2)-0.00682*exp(-((p)/0.09383)^2-((h-11.29138)/0.02985)^2)-0.00853*exp(-((p)/0.07677)^2-((h-11.22229)/0.03412)^2)+0.00341*exp(-((p)/0.09383)^2-((h-11.25897)/0.01024)^2)-0.01024*exp(-((p)/0.11942)^2-((h-11.00307)/0.05971)^2)
fy(p,h)=fpl(h)+fd(h)*(1-max(0,1-(p/fwd(h))^2)^fq(h))+fr(p,h)
# The mask is drawn as nine patches of the same surface, three across and three up: cheek, nose and
# mouth, cheek; eye, bridge of the nose, eye; and the brow. So the cheeks, nose, lips and chin each get
# their own fine mesh. Patches share their edges exactly, so no seam shows.
(0.81191*(fwd(h)*sin(f))+0.0572*(fpl(h)+fd(h)*(1-abs(cos(f))^(2*fq(h)))+fr(fwd(h)*sin(f),h))+(-0.09969)*(h)+1.11963,(-0.05677)*(fwd(h)*sin(f))+0.818*(fpl(h)+fd(h)*(1-abs(cos(f))^(2*fq(h)))+fr(fwd(h)*sin(f),h))+0.00697*(h)+(-0.05693),0.09993*(fwd(h)*sin(f))+0.81389*(h)+2.10307,f,-pi/2,(-0.36),h,10.92246,11.66) | ref=cheekRight color=#d4c2bb
